# Run Away Together's ruling (CR 608.2b): if one of the two targets becomes illegal, the spell still returns the other if it is a legal target, the one that
# left read as it last was to check it was controlled by a different player. On turn 3 Bot1 casts one copy on Ornithopter#1 and Bot2's Elvish Mystic,
# and in response a second on Ornithopter#2 and the same Mystic. The second resolves first, returning the Mystic and Ornithopter#2; the first then finds the Mystic gone
# but Ornithopter#1 still legal (Bot1 against the Mystic's last controller, Bot2), so it returns too.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Run Away Together
Run Away Together
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Run Away Together.Cast
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter#1; Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Run Away Together.Cast
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter#2; Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter; Ornithopter
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Island; Island
Bot2.Battlefield = Forest
Bot1.Graveyard = Run Away Together; Run Away Together
